                   DOCKER                                                              K8S

     - Builds containers                                                 - manages containers
    - runs containers                                                   - scales automatically
     - packages + dependencies                                          - handles failures
     - works on one meachine                                            - runs across  meachines
--> docker creates containers ,k8s manages them

KUBERNATES - kubectl
  its a container orchistration tool using which all the underlying different types of containers can be managed
  
docker kubectl differ
  docker is a docker container orchistration tool which means the commands only works when the underlying containers are all docker containers but kubctl can work 
  on any kind of containers and it can manage a huge no. of containers at a time by load balancing,scaling,replicaset

KIND installation :

  curl -Lo ./kind https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/dl/latest/kind-linux-amd64
chmod +x ./kind
sudo mv ./kind /usr/local/bin/kind

 kubectl installation : kubectl manages cluster

  sudo apt install kubectl -y or sudo snap install kubectl --classic

cluster creation :

 kind create cluster 

verifying:
  kubectl get nodes
